&lt;h1&gt;Hardware Design Senior Manager&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Bristol, UK&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About the job&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lead the engineers behind the power, timing and control circuits that make Graphcore’s AI compute hardware work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your team’s schematics, component choices and electrical constraints will give PCB layout engineers complete inputs for implementing each design. You’ll help test and manufacturing teams understand expected behaviour, resolve circuit issues and take hardware through to production.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll line-manage engineers, coach their development and agree achievable commitments, matching the work to available capacity. You’ll coordinate reviews and investigations, ensure corrective actions reach closure and plan ahead for tools, licences and compute resources.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Grow your leadership across the hardware lifecycle, drawing on specialist expertise rather than becoming the technical authority for every circuit. Build a more autonomous team whose methods and shared knowledge improve how Graphcore develops its next generation of hardware.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;The team and culture&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll connect Hardware Design with SI/PI, PCB layout, mechanical, thermal, systems and firmware engineers across locations. Programme management owns the integrated plan; you’ll flag competing priorities early and bring practical options for resolving them.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Technical owners help agree operating conditions, margins and acceptance criteria. You’ll encourage engineers to challenge assumptions, using evidence and specialist advice to resolve difficult trade-offs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What we’re looking for&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;People leadership that develops engineers, delegates effectively and addresses difficult performance issues, with readiness for formal line management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience coordinating engineering delivery with programme management, including estimates, work allocation, dependencies and capacity, with sound judgement under schedule pressure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communication that builds relationships across disciplines and locations, resolves competing expectations and secures decisions by explaining risks and trade-offs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong hardware engineering background spanning circuit and schematic development, board implementation, verification and production transition. An engineering degree or equivalent practical experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of power supplies, sequencing, reset, clocks, digital interfaces and SI/PI constraints, with judgement about when specialist input is needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience organising technical reviews, maintaining traceable design records and ensuring investigations and corrective actions reach a clear conclusion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;While we have outlined a set of requirements, we value transferable skills and diverse experiences. We also welcome engineers returning to the profession after a career break, including through returnship routes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Benefits&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;· Flexible working: Balance your work and personal life with greater flexibility&lt;br&gt;· Generous leave: Take time to rest, recharge and enjoy life outside of work&lt;br&gt;· Retirement planning support: Up to 5% matched pension&lt;br&gt;· Phantom equity: Share in Graphcore’s success&lt;br&gt;· Workplace experience: Enjoy thoughtfully designed office spaces for collaboration, with free food and an on-site barista to support your day&lt;br&gt;· Peace of mind protection: Income protection and life assurance to provide financial security for you and your loved ones&lt;br&gt;· Electric Vehicle Scheme: Choose an electric vehicle and lease it through salary sacrifice&lt;br&gt;· Flexible benefits: Tailor your benefits package with a choice of additional options, including private medical insurance and dental cover&lt;br&gt;· Optional benefits: Dental cover, health cash plan, private medical insurance, cycle to work scheme, give as you earn&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We welcome people from all backgrounds and experiences and are committed to building an inclusive environment where everyone can do their best work.&lt;br&gt;We’re an equal opportunity employer and recognise that everyone brings different strengths and perspectives. If you need any adjustments during the interview process, just let us know - we’re happy to support you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Sponsorship&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Applicants must have the legal right to work in the UK. Unfortunately, we are unable to provide visa sponsorship or support visa applications for this role.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Join the Team at Graphcore&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Graphcore is one of the world’s leading innovators in Artificial Intelligence compute. It is developing hardware, software and systems infrastructure that will unlock the next generation of AI breakthroughs and power the widespread adoption of AI solutions across every industry.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As part of the SoftBank Group, Graphcore is a member of an elite family of companies responsible for some of the world’s most transformative technologies. Together, they share a bold vision: to enable Artificial Super Intelligence and ensure its benefits are accessible to everyone.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Graphcore’s teams are drawn from diverse backgrounds and bring a broad range of skills and perspectives. A melting pot of AI research specialists, silicon designers, software engineers and systems architects, Graphcore brings together deep expertise to solve complex problems and deliver meaningful progress in AI compute.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ready to lead the engineers shaping Graphcore’s AI compute hardware? Apply for the Hardware Design Team Lead role in Bristol.&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;At Hudl, we build great teams. We hire the best of the best to ensure you’re working with people you can constantly learn from. You’re trusted to get your work done your way while testing the limits of what’s possible and what’s next. We work hard to provide a culture where everyone feels supported, and our employees feel it—their votes helped us become one of the &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.hudl.com/blog/hudl-2026-top-100-inspiring-workplaces?utm_medium=internal&amp;amp;utm_source=job-ad&amp;amp;utm_campaign=26_NA_talent_job-ad&amp;amp;utm_content=1org_learn-more_blog-link_learn-more_2blog_organic_3ctw&quot;&gt;Top 100 Inspiring Workplaces&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We think of ourselves as the team behind the team, supporting the lifelong impact sports can have: the lessons in teamwork and dedication; the influence of inspiring coaches; and the opportunities to reach new heights. That’s why we help teams from all over the world see their game differently. Our products make it easier for coaches and athletes at any level to capture video, analyze data, share highlights and more.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Ready to join us?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div style=&quot;padding: 56.25% 0 0 0; position: relative;&quot;&gt;&lt;iframe style=&quot;position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; border: 0;&quot; src=&quot;https://player.vimeo.com/video/1095624224?h=9e8cdc9dbe&amp;amp;badge=0&amp;amp;autopause=0&amp;amp;player_id=0&amp;amp;app_id=58479&quot; width=&quot;&quot; height=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Your Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re hiring a Senior Quality Assurance Engineer to join our Core Video &amp;amp; Data team, where quality work supports the platform athletes and coaches rely on to train, compete, and improve. This team builds the systems that power how Hudl understands sport at scale; from identifying players and teams across thousands of leagues to processing the moments that become highlights, stats and analysis, our services sit at the center of Hudl&#39;s platform. The systems you build won&#39;t support just one product or one sport, they&#39;ll become shared capabilities used across Hudl&#39;s ecosystem, powering experiences for teams, athletes and fans around the world.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the Senior QA, you’ll;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Shape our quality strategy:&lt;/strong&gt; You will use your customer and system understanding to build a risk-based testing approach tailored to our video and data platform architecture. You will measure quality to help define when a project is truly complete and prove your improvements with real, data-backed results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead quality in your squad:&lt;/strong&gt; As an integral part of a cross-functional team across Engineering, Product, Design, and Scrum, you will guide quality-focused conversations in sprint ceremonies. You will partner with stakeholders to explain how defects affect users and advocate for the right priority on backlog defects before they enter a sprint.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Test at scale and automate:&lt;/strong&gt; Aligning our processes with development speed, you will make informed decisions on what, how, and when to automate versus when to rely on manual testing. You will lead large testing efforts, bringing your knowledge of our users into every test plan.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Coach and elevate the team:&lt;/strong&gt; You will use your technical and quality expertise to guide others and raise the team&#39;s overall bar. As the quality point person, you will influence and challenge teams to incorporate best practices in everything they do.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Time spent collaborating with your teammates in-office will be a regular part of how you work. We&#39;re currently considering applicants within commuting distance of London. You&#39;ll be expected to work more days in-office than remote, but will have the freedom to coordinate your specific in-office schedule with your team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Must-Haves&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experienced.&lt;/strong&gt; You have deep full-stack testing experience alongside an in-depth knowledge of automation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Quality leadership.&lt;/strong&gt; You understand quality in the big picture. You’ve successfully led quality initiatives and projects, and know exactly what success looks like at the project level.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;User-focused.&lt;/strong&gt; You think critically about the user experience, making sure our testing approach adapts seamlessly to match user workflows and exceed expectations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Risk-aware.&lt;/strong&gt; You can design a testing approach that effectively reduces risk, and you bring the sharp attention to detail necessary to catch what others miss.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Nice-to-Haves&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Playwright Experience:&lt;/strong&gt; Commercial experience with Playwright is a major plus, as this is one of our core frameworks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A STEM Degree.&lt;/strong&gt; A bachelor’s degree or equivalent is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;HowtoWriteaJobAdvert/JobAdvertisement-WeWill(heading2,bolded)&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Champion work-life harmony&lt;/strong&gt;. We’ll give you the flexibility you need in your work life (e.g., flexible vacation time above any required statutory leave, company-wide holidays, remote work options and more) so you can enjoy your personal life too.&amp;nbsp; Plus, every five years, we give you a paid sabbatical to unplug and recharge.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Guarantee autonomy&lt;/strong&gt;. We have an open, honest culture and we trust our people from day one. Your team will support you, but you’ll own your work and have the agency to try new ideas.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Encourage career growth. &lt;/strong&gt;We’re lifelong learners who encourage professional development. We’ll give you tons of resources and opportunities to keep growing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Provide an environment to help you succeed&lt;/strong&gt;. We&#39;ve invested in our offices, designing incredible spaces with our employees in mind. But whether you’re at the office or working remotely, we’ll provide you the tech you need to do your best work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Support your wellbeing. &lt;/strong&gt;Depending on location, we offer medical and retirement benefits for employees—but no matter where you’re located, we have resources like our Employee Assistance Program and employee resource groups to support your mental health.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Compensation&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;The base salary range for this role is displayed below—&lt;strong&gt;starting salaries will typically fall near the middle of this range.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We make compensation decisions based on an individual&#39;s experience, skills and education in line with our internal pay equity practices.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role will also be eligible for a long-term incentive (LTI) award. Any bonuses awarded are based on individual and company performance paid at Hudl&#39;s discretion.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Base Salary Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;£66,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;£111,000 GBP&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Privacy Policy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.hudl.com/jobs/hudl-applicant-and-candidate-privacy-policy&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Hudl Applicant and Candidate Privacy Policy&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Wheely&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Wheely is redefining premium transportation across major cities in Europe, the US, and the Middle East. We blend cutting-edge technology with the craft of five-star chauffeuring to deliver an experience trusted by more than 100,000 active riders and 1,200 corporate accounts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re a profitable, fast-growing scale-up with $43M raised and over $100M in annual revenue. Having recently launched in New York City, we’re expanding rapidly across the US and EMEA. If you take pride in your craft and want to help shape the next chapter of our growth, we&#39;d love to hear from you.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;About the Role&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a&lt;strong&gt; Senior Operations Manager in Paris&lt;/strong&gt;, you&#39;ll be a senior member of the France Operations team, reporting to the General Manager, France. You&#39;ll own the day-to-day health of the market — acquiring, retaining, and driving quality among our best-in-class chauffeurs — and help evolve the local operating model as we scale beyond Paris.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is an entrepreneurial, high-ownership role in a fast-moving environment, not a caretaker seat.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Why This Role&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;High-growth business.&lt;/strong&gt; Paris is scaling and we&#39;re actively expanding into new markets — you&#39;ll help shape how we operate as we grow.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Direct impact.&lt;/strong&gt; Chauffeur acquisition, supply and retention — your calls move the metrics that define the market&#39;s health.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Real ownership.&lt;/strong&gt; You&#39;ll build and lead the local ops team, processes, and operating rhythms yourself, not inherit someone else&#39;s.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own day-to-day operational execution: chauffeur supply growth and retention.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evolve the local operating model, turning global strategy and standards into effective execution on the ground.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use data to spot operational risks and opportunities, and design initiatives with clear, measurable impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and grow Wheely Paris&#39;s operations team, building a culture of high performance and engagement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with product teams to shape feature development and improve operational tooling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support readiness as the market expands into new areas, launching business from scratch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a senior point of contact for chauffeurs and key external stakeholders, representing Wheely&#39;s standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure compliance with applicable French regulations and VTC licensing requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;No single background defines success here — we want analytically strong, entrepreneurial operators motivated by ownership and comfortable being accountable for outcomes in open-ended environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3-4+ years building, growing, or scaling something meaningful with limited structure, with the ability to move fast from analysis to execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Relevant backgrounds include:&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;scaling operations in a fast-paced tech environment (VC-backed business, scale-up, startup);&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;top-tier management consulting, investment banking, or VC/PE; early or founding-team experience at a consumer or marketplace startup.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus points:&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;experience in a marketplace/platform business (on-demand, mobility, location-based);&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;track record building teams or operating models from scratch or through rapid expansion;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;MBA or advanced degree in business, operations, analytics, or strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent French and English.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Based in Paris, ability to work in the office 4 days a week.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What we Offer&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Office-based role in Paris (9th arrondissement)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive salary&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employee stock options plan&lt;/li&gt;
